{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011bXJikALoiUUp3y6x5Bn8U","type":"tool_result","content":"55:**1.** A container and a virtual machine both run an application in isolation from the host's other workloads. Which statement correctly distinguishes them?\n64:**2.** Which Kubernetes component is the only one that writes to cluster state?\n73:**3.** A Deployment's `.spec.replicas` is set to 5. An administrator manually deletes one of the five Pods. What happens next, and which component is responsible?\n82:**4.** A Pod manifest sets a container's memory request to `256Mi` and its memory limit to `512Mi`. Which QoS class does the Pod receive, assuming this is its only container?\n91:**5.** An image is referenced as `registry.example.com/team/api:v2`. The same tag is later pushed again, pointing at different content. Which statement is true?\n100:**6.** Which statement about a Kubernetes Namespace is correct?\n109:**7.** A CNI plugin has not been installed on a freshly bootstrapped cluster. What is the most likely observed symptom?\n118:**8.** A Service of type `ClusterIP` selects Pods with the label `app: web`. Three Pods carry that label; one of them is failing its readiness probe. How many endpoints does the Service have?\n127:**9.** Which of the following is the CNCF's stated purpose for the KCNA-level tier of certification, as reflected in the curriculum's own description?\n136:**10.** A `helm rollback` and a `kubectl rollout undo` both move a workload backward. Which statement correctly distinguishes them?\n145:**11.** Which statement about a StatefulSet is the reason it exists as a separate workload kind from a Deployment?\n154:**12.** ```yaml\n174:**13.** In the four-layer cloud native security model, which layer is the outermost — the one whose compromise undermines every layer inside it?\n183:**14.** An operator applies a NetworkPolicy that allows ingress to Pods labeled `app: db` from Pods labeled `app: api`, and a second NetworkPolicy that denies ingress from `app: batch`. What is the effect?\n192:**15.** A container reads its database password from a file mounted from a Secret. Which statement about that Secret is accurate?\n201:**16.** Which of the following is the correct order of the three gates every request to the API server passes through?\n210:**17.** A `kubectl get pods` shows a Pod with status `CrashLoopBackOff` and eleven restarts. Which command retrieves the output of the container run that most recently failed?\n219:**18.** Which statement describes GitOps as distinct from a conventional CI/CD pipeline?\n228:**19.** A Pod's container is terminated and the container state's `Reason` reads `OOMKilled`. What does this indicate?\n237:**20.** What does an Ingress object accomplish on a cluster where no Ingress controller is installed?\n246:**21.** Which of these is the durable, testable fact about the CNCF project maturity levels?\n255:**22.** An init container in a Pod exits with a non-zero status. What happens?\n264:**23.** A cluster administrator wants to take a node out of service for maintenance without losing the workloads running on it. Which sequence is correct?\n273:**24.** Which statement about the relationship between a Deployment, a ReplicaSet, and a Pod is correct?\n282:**25.** Which of the following best describes an operator in the Kubernetes sense?\n291:**26.** A PersistentVolumeClaim requests `ReadWriteOnce`. What does this constrain?\n300:**27.** Which of the following is true of `kubectl top pods` on a cluster where nothing beyond the core control plane has been installed?\n309:**28.** In a Helm chart, what is the role of `values.yaml`?\n318:**29.** A Pod has a liveness probe and a readiness probe, both HTTP GETs against different paths. The readiness probe begins failing while the liveness probe continues to succeed. What happens?\n327:**30.** Which describes the relationship between the four golden signals and the RED method?\n336:**31.** A taint is applied to a node with the effect `NoExecute`. What is the consequence for a running Pod on that node that does not tolerate the taint?\n345:**32.** A container image is built `FROM` a base image and adds two layers. A second image is built from the same base and adds one different layer. What does the registry store?\n354:**33.** Which statement about Kubernetes version skew is accurate?\n363:**34.** What distinguishes a headless Service from a standard ClusterIP Service?\n372:**35.** An organization wants configuration that varies between staging and production without maintaining two copies of the manifests, and prefers not to use templating. Which tool matches?\n381:**36.** A Pod that mounts an `emptyDir` volume is deleted and its controller recreates it on the same node. What happens to the data in the volume?\n390:**37.** Which statement about RBAC in Kubernetes is correct?\n399:**38.** What does the Container Runtime Interface standardize?\n408:**39.** A Deployment's rolling update is configured with `maxSurge: 1` and `maxUnavailable: 0` on a Deployment of four replicas. What is the maximum number of Pods that may exist during the update?\n417:**40.** Which is the correct characterization of Prometheus's data collection model?\n426:**41.** A cluster operator sets a ResourceQuota on a namespace limiting total memory requests to `10Gi`, and a LimitRange in the same namespace setting a default container memory request of `256Mi`. What does each accomplish?\n435:**42.** Which statement about `imagePullPolicy` is accurate?\n444:**43.** A DaemonSet is used to run a log-collection agent. Why is a DaemonSet the correct workload kind for this?\n453:**43 continues on the next item.**\n455:**44.** In a service mesh, what is the distinction between the data plane and the control plane?\n464:**45.** A cluster has 3 control plane nodes and 20 worker nodes. Where does the authoritative record of cluster state live?\n473:**46.** Which statement about labels and selectors is correct?\n482:**47.** A team wants to deploy a new version to a small subset of production traffic before committing to a full rollout. Which strategy names this?\n491:**48.** Which statement about the Kubernetes network model's requirements is correct?\n500:**49.** A distributed trace shows one request passing through four services. What is the unit representing a single operation within that trace?\n509:**50.** Which of the following is the correct expansion and meaning of SBOM?\n518:**51.** A CronJob is defined with `schedule: \"0 2 * * *\"`. What does it create when it fires?\n527:**52.** Which of the following most accurately describes what an admission controller does?\n536:**53.** A Pod is stuck with the container-state reason `ImagePullBackOff`. Which of these is *not* a plausible cause?\n545:**54.** What does an Argo CD `Application` in state `OutOfSync` indicate?\n554:**55.** Which statement about scale-to-zero, as offered by Knative, is correct?\n563:**56.** A cluster's storage is provisioned on demand when a PersistentVolumeClaim is created, without an administrator pre-creating volumes. What makes this possible?\n572:**57.** A developer needs a shell inside a running container whose image contains no shell — a distroless build. Which approach fits?\n581:**58.** Which statement about immutable infrastructure as a cloud native principle is correct?\n590:**59.** A microservices architecture is chosen over a monolith. Which trade-off is the honest characterization?\n599:**60.** Which of the following is the accurate statement about how a Kubernetes controller behaves?\n618:**1. B** — *D1.4 · Ch 2 §1 · ⚪*\n628:**2. C** — *D1.1 · Ch 3 §5 · 🔵*\n638:**3. B** — *D1.1 · Ch 6 §1 · ⚪*\n648:**4. B** — *D1.1 · Ch 5 §8 · 🔵*\n658:**5. B** — *D1.4 · Ch 2 §3 · 🔵*\n668:**6. B** — *D1.1 · Ch 4 §3 · ⚪*\n678:**7. B** — *D2.1 · Ch 9 §1 · 🔵*\n688:**8. B** — *D2.1 · Ch 9 §4 · 🔵*\n698:**9. B** — *D4.2 · Ch 17 §2 · ⚪*","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c1f0b